@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-dial-requires-actor-authority
Guest terminal dials MUST use an identity obtained from the VM actor for the
current durable running placement/epoch/generation. For a restored checkpoint,
the hello proof MUST use its verified original guest placement, epoch and boot
challenge; that guest tuple MUST NOT authorize the current host execution.
The actor authorizes only the assigned terminal stream process.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-attach-requires-fresh-hello
Every guest attachment connection MUST complete its own fresh boot-bound HMAC
hello before presenting the session token or carrying terminal bytes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] terminal-input-dedup-before-delivery
Stream input frames MUST be applied only with a strictly increasing
per-channel sequence; equal or older sequences MUST be dropped without
delivery so stream reconnects can never execute guest input twice.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-bytes-never-in-diagnostics
Terminal bytes, titles and replay payloads MUST NOT enter logs, GenServer
status reports or crash reports. Process status carries identifiers and
counters only.
